record('air-india-talace','Air India: follow the sale cash, acquired debt and public cleanup separately','Tata Sons→Talace acquired the public airline. The government actually received₹2,700cr;₹15,300cr debt stayed inside the acquired airlines. Excluded non-core assets valued₹14,718cr went to the public holding perimeter. The later Union Budget reports₹62,365.40cr actual FY22 equity to AIAHL—₹308.40cr above the prior₹62,057cr estimate, driven by the past-dues component. These are different ledgers, not quantities to net into an unsupported “giveaway”.',['air-india-award','air-india-close','air-budget-2022','air-budget-actual-2023'],['goi','tata-sons','talace','air-india','aiahl','ajay-singh-consortium'],[e['id'] for e in D['relationships'] if e['recordIds']==aircase],AIR,['organisations','funding','procurement','policy','review'],'2021-10-08','2023-02-01','Award8-Oct2021; closing27-Jan2022; actual FY2021–22 expenditure published1-Feb2023','Government says excessive losses/debt required an EV bidding model to improve competition, two bids exceeded reserve, and guarantees were to be released before closing. The record contains no adjudicated corruption finding.',['A loss-making airline may require balance-sheet cleanup to obtain competitive bids; historical creditor repayment is not automatically a benefit created for the buyer.','₹14,718cr is asset valuation, not monetisation revenue, and cannot be subtracted as if realised.','Actual expenditure differs from the prior estimate; the difference is a normal reconciliation question until creditor-level evidence explains it.'],'Obtain AIAHL audited ledger and creditor settlements, SPA schedules, independent valuation and realised asset-sale receipts; these could establish which liabilities/assets transferred and test any claimed net public cost.',amounts=[amount(2700,'sale cash actually received','2022-01-27'),amount(15300,'debt retained in acquired airlines','2022-01-27'),amount(62365.4,'actual government equity infusion into AIAHL','FY2021–22'),amount(62057,'prior revised estimate; not an additional payment','FY2021–22')],status='sale-completed; public-expenditure-reconciled-to-budget-actual',end='2023-02-01',limits=['No buyer-specific loan write-off or waiver is established. No post2022 ownership continuity is assumed.','Budget expenditure to AIAHL does not establish the date or amount of every creditor payment.'])

